netfilter: nft_set_pipapo: clamp maximum map bucket size to INT_MAX

jira KERNEL-1646
cve CVE-2025-38201
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8
commit-author Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
commit b85e3367a5716ed3662a4fe266525190d2af76df
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8/b85e3367.failed

Otherwise, it is possible to hit WARN_ON_ONCE in __kvmalloc_node_noprof()
when resizing hashtable because __GFP_NOWARN is unset.

Similar to:

  b541ba7d1f5a ("netfilter: conntrack: clamp maximum hashtable size to INT_MAX")

	Reviewed-by: Stefano Brivio <sbrivio@redhat.com>
	Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
(cherry picked from commit b85e3367a5716ed3662a4fe266525190d2af76df)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

